1u64|v|To strip or break off the shell of; to take out of the shell, pod, etc.; as, to shell nuts or pease; to shell oysters. ; To separate the kernels of (an ear of Indian corn, wheat, oats, etc.) from the cob, ear, or husk. ; To throw shells or bombs upon or into; to bombard; as, to shell a town. ; To fall off, as a shell, crust, etc. ; To cast the shell, or exterior covering; to fall out of the pod or husk; as, nuts shell in falling. ; To be disengaged from the ear or husk; as, wheat or rye shells in reaping.	s:13q8,5,2~13q8,5,2	d:8sq,6,1~8sq,6,1
